<BaseLayout title="Privacy & Cookies" description="Privacy and cookie information for Ze-Xun Lai — Environmental Intelligence."><article><header class="page-intro reading"><span class="eyebrow">Legal</span><h1>Privacy & Cookies</h1><p>How this website handles information, infrastructure and browser storage.</p><div class="meta">Last updated 15 Sep 2026</div></header><div class="reading prose"><h2>Website operator</h2><p>This personal professional knowledge platform is operated by Ze-Xun Lai.</p><h2>Information collected</h2><p>If you use the contact form, the name, email address, subject and message you submit are stored so I can respond. Basic technical data may be processed for security and rate limiting. The private owner login stores authentication session cookies required to protect the administration area.</p><h2>Purpose and handling</h2><p>Contact information is used only to respond to the conversation you initiated. It is not sold or used for advertising. Contact records can be reviewed and deleted by the site owner.</p><h2>Infrastructure and translation</h2><p>GitHub hosts the website code. Cloudflare delivers and runs the website. Supabase provides the content database, private owner authentication and storage for website-owned media. When the owner requests machine translation, editorial content is sent server-side to Google Cloud Translation; Google credentials remain private and the site records translation provenance. These providers may process technical request information under their respective privacy terms.</p><h2>Cookies, local storage and analytics</h2><p>Public pages do not use advertising cookies, behavioural tracking or Google Analytics. Authentication cookies apply only to the private owner login. No cookie banner is shown because the site does not use non-essential tracking.</p><h2>Correction or deletion requests</h2><p>Use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> to request access, correction or deletion of information you submitted.</p><h2>Changes</h2><p>This notice will be updated when the website’s actual data handling changes.</p></div></article></BaseLayout><style>article{padding-bottom:110px}.page-intro h1{font-size:clamp(3rem,7vw,6rem)}.meta{color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem}</style>
